  ('studying-without-the-stress', 85, 'Set up a simple folder system on your computer: one folder per course, one subfolder per unit.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 86, 'Pick a stopping cue for each study session, like the end of a page or the bottom of a problem set.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 87, 'Bring a water bottle and a sweater to the library so a cold room doesn''t cut your session short.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 88, 'Write your study goal for this session as one sentence, like "I can explain photosynthesis in my own words."'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 89, 'Within a day of your class, reread that day''s notes and add one question in the margin.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 90, 'Record yourself explaining a concept on your phone, then play it back and listen for the fuzzy parts.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 91, 'Sort your flashcards into two piles, the ones you know and the ones you don''t, and study the second pile.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 92, 'Look up one video or diagram that explains a topic from a different angle than your textbook.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 93, 'Write a practice exam question for yourself, then come back in an hour and answer it.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 94, 'Turn your notes for one lecture into a one-page outline with headings and short bullet phrases.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 95, 'Ask a friend to quiz you for ten minutes using your flashcards or textbook questions.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 96, 'Space out your review: look at today''s flashcards again tonight, then again in two days.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 97, 'Pick one study method you''ve never tried, like mind mapping or the Cornell note format, and give it one session.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 98, 'Draw a timeline of the events or steps you need to know for one topic.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 99, 'Find the answer key or worked solutions for one problem set and compare them with your own work.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 100, 'Choose one paragraph of a dense reading and translate it into plain, everyday language.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 101, 'Make a list of the words you need to know for one unit and write a short definition beside each one.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 102, 'Practice writing an essay outline in fifteen minutes, as if it were a timed exam question.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 103, 'Compare your notes with a classmate''s and add anything you missed.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 104, 'Read your assignment rubric or grading guide and check one piece of your work against it.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 105, 'Try the Feynman approach: write a one-paragraph explanation of a concept a twelve-year-old could follow.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 106, 'For a class, a course or something you''re teaching yourself, list the three topics that feel shakiest right now.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 107, 'Redo one problem you got wrong earlier, without looking at the correction until you''ve finished.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 108, 'Work in short bursts today: three sessions of fifteen minutes, with a real break between each.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 109, 'Visit office hours with one specific question, even if you think it''s a small one.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 110, 'Email your instructor a short, polite question about something that confused you in class.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 111, 'Make a study plan for one exam that fits on an index card: topics on the left, dates on the right.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 112, 'Pick a quiet cafe for one study session and order something warm to drink while you work.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 113, 'Agree with a study partner to work side by side on a video call for thirty quiet minutes.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 114, 'Highlight in one color only the terms you''d want on a flashcard, then make those cards right away.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 115, 'Say the steps of a process out loud while you walk around the room.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 116, 'Look for patterns across three practice problems and write down what they have in common.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 117, 'Use the last five minutes of a session to write what still confuses you, for next time.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 118, 'Find a past exam or sample questions for your course and read through them without answering yet.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 119, 'Teach a concept to a pet, a plant or a stuffed animal, out loud, start to finish.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 120, 'Cover the answers in your notes with a sheet of paper and test yourself line by line.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 121, 'Write down how long you think one task will take, then time it and compare.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 122, 'Make one flashcard that connects two ideas from different chapters.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 123, 'Study one topic at the kitchen table today if your desk has started to feel stale.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 124, 'Choose the single most useful thing to study tonight and do that before anything else.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 125, 'Put a small plant, a photo or something you like to look at on your study desk.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 126, 'Notice when your attention drifts during reading, and gently bring it back to the next sentence.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 127, 'Keep a scrap paper beside you for stray thoughts, so they leave your head and you can return to the page.'),
  ('studying-without-the-stress', 128, 'Plan a short reward for after tonight''s session, like an episode of a show or a call with a friend.'),
